     {
      "text": "49-year-old male presenting with headache with dizziness for 3 days. Character: throbbing at the back of the head; radiation: to the neck; aggravated by morning time; relieved by rest. Severity 6/10. Associated: palpitations. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 7 years; Hypertension for 11 years; Appendectomy in 2019. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: hypertension. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
